{"revision": 26, "recorded_at": "2026-10-23T03:24:20Z", "stage": "T10 settled; next ready task T11; readiness P04 step 2: escalated commits wait for the operator's SEA-Forge approval (J02 IS3-IS5 live)", "summary": "Readiness P04 step 2 (no spec change): with SEA-Forge governance, a navigation commit runs as the Cognate run horizon.navigation.commit, so SEA-Forge's escalate parks it on a durable governance approval instead of failing. submitIntent throws AwaitingAuthorityError (audited as awaiting_authority; POST /intent answers 202); resolveNavigationApproval records the human operator's decision at SEA-Forge (on_behalf_of the operator named by COGNATE_SEA_FORGE_OPERATOR), and on resume SEA-Forge revalidates and the run writes the record. appendIntentRecord is now exactly-once per intent_id (store idempotency key plus a stream check): the same intent returns the first record, a different intent under that id is duplicate_intent (already_exists, audited). The capability docs had promised this guard, but no code implemented it. The teeth fake runtime gains governanceFromEnv, so the fake-runtime tooth fails the E2E on behaviour again (Horizon #1 had made the test file fail to load). Revision 25's evidence field was malformed (a path split into characters); this entry lists it correctly.", "verified": ["test/J02-live.test.ts (real sea-forge-server): 2 pass. Escalate -> AwaitingAuthorityError with apr- id, no record, awaiting_authority audited; the service identity's self-approval is refused (cep_approval_refused); the operator's approval commits exactly once and the approval is 'used'; a second resolution fails and a resubmission returns the same record; a rejection commits nothing and is audited refused", "mutation: without the governed run, the escalation is not parked (test fails); without the SEA-Forge resolution (poll only), the run stays waiting and nothing commits (test fails); a hand resume of the continuation is refused by Horizon's action policy", "test/app.t