{"revision": 27, "recorded_at": "2026-10-23T03:35:06Z", "stage": "T10 settled; next ready task T11; readiness P04 step 2: escalated commits wait for the operator's SEA-Forge approval (J02 IS3-IS5 live)", "summary": "Review fixes for readiness P04 step 2 (Horizon #2). The exactly-once guard is an index record keyed <tenant>/<intent_id>, written with the intent event (expected version 0), so the duplicate check is one record read instead of a scan of every intent, is atomic, and is tenant-scoped; intents recorded before the index are indexed once per process. On the governed path a reused intent id is duplicate_intent and audited (it leaked Cognate's raw already_exists). Horizon polls SEA-Forge for decisions (approvalPollMs 2000 by default), so an approval made at SEA-Forge directly still resumes the commit, and the run audits its own acceptance; answering an already-decided approval again is refused. Run polling backs off (5 ms to 200 ms). The SEA-Forge client closes its socket on timeout and decodes UTF-8 in stream mode. Readiness P04 step 2 (no spec change): with SEA-Forge governance, a navigation commit runs as the Cognate run horizon.navigation.commit, so SEA-Forge's escalate parks it on a durable governance approval instead of failing. submitIntent throws AwaitingAuthorityError (audited as awaiting_authority; POST /intent answers 202); resolveNavigationApproval records the human operator's decision at SEA-Forge (on_behalf_of the operator named by COGNATE_SEA_FORGE_OPERATOR), and on resume SEA-Forge revalidates and the run writes the record. appendIntentRecord is now exactly-once per intent_id (store idempotency key plus a stream check): the same intent returns the first record, a different intent under that id is duplicate_intent (already_exists, audited). The capability docs had promised this guard, but no code implemented it. The teeth fake runtime gains governanceFromEnv, so the fake-runtime tooth fails the E2E on behaviour again (Horizon #1 had made the test file fail to load). Revision 25's evidence field was malformed (a path split into characters); this entry lists it correctly.", "verified": ["test/J02-live.test.ts (real sea-forge-server): 2 pass; the escalation test now also covers governed duplicate_intent (audited) and an approval made at SEA-Forge directly (resumed by polling, audited awaiting_authority then accepted, a second answer refused)", "mutations: approvalPollMs 0 -> the directly-approved commit never resumes (fails); index lookup disabled -> exactly-once test fails; backfill disabled -> legacy-intent test fails; earlier mutations (no governed run; no SEA-Forge resolution) still hold", "test/app.test.ts: exactly-once and legacy-intent tests pass", "bun test: 141 pass / 2 skip (live, opt-in) / 0 fail", "bun x tsc --noEmit: exit 0", "just check, boundaries, idm-integrity, acceptance-claims, witness-claims, ledger, wayfinder, teeth: all exit 0"], "limits": ["The frame register is in memory: a commit approved after a restart, or after a newer frame was issued, fails as a stale intent; an approval never revives a stale frame", "Approval resolution mirrors Cognate-Workbench's seaForgeCall because Cognate 0.6.2 exports none (readiness debt: export it from Cognate)", "No HTTP route answers an approval: that would need Workbench-style Host/Origin guards; resolution is an application call for the operator", "IS6 (RealityTrace observation, settlement reference) and IS2/IS7 (SPEC-CR candidate) remain", "An escalation rejected at SEA-Forge directly fails the run (nothing is committed) but its refusal is audited only when Horizon next settles that run (resolveNavigationApproval)"], "next": "Readiness P04 step 3: RealityTrace observation outbox and SEA-Forge settlement reference (IS6); then the J02 gate in godspeed-readiness. T11 remains the next spec task.", "decisions": ["DEC-T10-A", "DEC-T10-B", "DEC-T10-C"], "evidence": [".agents/evidence/horizon/T10/SUMMARY.md", "test/J02-live.test.ts", "test/app.test.ts", "~/pr