istrations promised. The fifth independent review (frozen-round-5, manifest verified by the reviewer, exit 0, every file OK) returned REJECT with six blocking and three must-fix findings. It called seven of the nine round-4 findings CLOSED (the first wave whose corrections it could close outright) and two PARTIALLY CLOSED. The six blocking findings are: five reachable desktop P3 rows perform their effects although the live-enforcement table admits they lack the pending/A3/authority path; run.start is an authority-free Px dispatcher whose target resolution is named missing but whose handler sends an unclassified case_advance; a device credential is converted into a human actor by the remote server and the human commit path; the agent_execution executor is mapped to registered_agent_key although the live agent door authenticates only the stable key; the record contract's caller kinds neither cover nor verify the catalog's executors, and live validation never proves a record's caller_kind is permitted for its operation; and the remaining published authority interface is a composite that lists conditional owner fields as unqualified requirements, omits the Merkle inclusion-proof fields, binds no Horizon reference to an owner field, and coexists with local signed payloads that read like owner artifacts. The three must-fix findings are: class inheritance gives P0/P1 rows assurance predicates the public and pairing routes cannot produce; 'before any record is appended' and performs:false are false because refusals append an audit; and the P3 class rule asserts separation of duty universally while only three rows set it.", "verified": ["bun test: 1563 pass, 16 skip, 0 fail across 176 files (11717 expect() calls)", "bun test test/identity-remediation-3.test.ts: 18 pass, 0 fail, 193 expect() calls", "bun test test/identity-contract.test.ts: 69 pass, 0 fail", "bun test test/identity-records.test.ts: 31 pass, 0 fail", "bun test test/identity-defects.test.ts: 14 pass, 0 fail", "